{
  "question": "What is the NYC micropurchase limit for goods and services?",
  "status": "answered",
  "answer": "The New York City micropurchase limit for goods and all services except construction is $20,000 or less. For procurements of construction, the micropurchase limit is $35,000 or less. Under this rule, no competition is required for purchases below these limits.",
